<title>INDIA: Central Indian soybean markets shut in protest.</title>
<headline>Central Indian soybean markets shut in protest.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>All soybean markets remained closed in central India for indefinite period. Traders closed their business in protest against the increase in the mandi (market) tax from one percent to two percent. Traders were demanding government to take back increased tax which was imposed from 1st May 97.</p>
</text>
